      "content": "fair enough, good point on the hardware stuff. \n\nlet's dig a bit deeper into the \"cultural\" side of things then. as we build these out, i want to make sure our marketing and persona building matches the UI. if we're leaning into that \"energetic/information-dense\" look for the Lagos segment, should we be portraying them as more community-oriented or perhaps more \"hustle\" driven in our copy? \n\nand for the Tokyo/Dubai crowd, since you mentioned they favor minimalism/tranquility, should we be styling the actual user imagery and brand voice to feel more reserved and elite? just trying to figure out if these design choices imply a certain \"level\" of user sophistication that differs between these regions.",
